[{"id":"0d65cf49-0d78-4c97-93ac-93c89ec042f7","filename":"1.1 Definitions.pdf","status":"indexed","page_count":2,"chunk_count":3,"chunks":[{"text":"Definitions: Definitions of: Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Deep Learning & Generative AI Hierarchy: Artificial Intelligence (AI) │ └── Machine Learning (ML) │ └── Deep Learning (DL) │ └── Genera Ɵ ve AI (Gen AI) Each one is a subset of the one before it — narrowing in scope but increasing in capability for specific tasks (especially content creation, in Gen AI's case). Layer Definition Example 1 Example 2 AI Learning to Simulate human intelligence Google Maps Siri/Alexa ML Learning to Predict/Classify using data patterns Spam filters Netflix recommendations DL Learning to Extract features automatically using neural networks Face unlock Google Translate Gen AI Learning to Create/Generate new content ChatGPT/Claude DALL·E 1. Artificial Intelligence (AI) The broad field of building machines/systems that can perform tasks requiring human-like intelligence — such as reasoning, learning, understanding language, and decision-making. AI is the umbrella concept — machines simulating human intelligence. Examples:  Google Maps – uses AI for route optimization and traffic prediction  Siri/Alexa – AI-powered virtual assistants that understand and respond to voice commands","page_number":1,"embedding":[0.0007357186,0.08305527,-0.1308396,-0.038908154,0.080599055,0.046390764,0.019035907,-0.034408,-0.03165695,0.017243141,-0.02807971,0.044823553,0.105142705,0.050101962,0.00027566924,-0.065940395,-0.032612655,-0.010145103,0.009676721,0.0027149527,0.0012664914,-0.0069773253,0.017956289,0.0018146961,0.020283125,-0.00036272348,-0.038297255,-0.04823844,-0.0022374918,-0.029085178,-0.022495389,-0.027682586,0.02343371,0.019960724,-0.05023678,-0.034579743,0.073747315,0.027256804,0.025160773,0.033358976,-0.0008658823,0.0322578,0.003781762,-0.017013105,0.015259668,0.030075919,-0.011698143,-0.040710624,0.087758645,-0.0625496,0.03595782